  "stream": {
    "_doc": "SPEC §8 'In-process models' + §8C 'Streaming'. Real incremental streaming through the in-process seam and the ACP transport. Every port replays both cases. A faked stream (the whole answer buffered and re-emitted, or one chunk) MUST fail them: inProcess blocks the generate until the consumer has observed each delta, and acpDrip spaces its chunks in time and asserts the first delta lands well before done.",
    "inProcess": {
      "_doc": "A streaming generate (Go GenerateStream; idiomatic name per port) is driven through client.stream. After emitting each text delta the generate WAITS (up to waitMs) until the consumer has received that delta; if it never does the generate fails with notIncrementalError. Non-text events pass straight to the consumer and are never executed by the loop.",
      "prompt": "q",
      "waitMs": 5000,
      "emits": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "delta": "al",
          "awaitConsumer": true
        },
        {
          "type": "thought",
          "delta": "hmm",
          "via": "acp"
        },
        {
          "type": "tool_call",
          "id": "t1",
          "name": "reading files",
          "args": {},
          "via": "acp"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "delta": "pha",
          "awaitConsumer": true
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "content": "alpha"
      },
      "expectTextDeltas": [
        "al",
        "pha"
      ],
      "expectPassThrough": [
        {
          "type": "thought",
          "delta": "hmm",
          "via": "acp"
        },
        {
          "type": "tool_call",
          "id": "t1",
          "name": "reading files",
          "via": "acp"
        }
      ],
      "expectDoneText": "alpha",
      "expectDoneToolCalls": 0,
      "notIncrementalError": "stream not incremental: consumer never saw the delta",
      "plainGenerateStillRefuses": true
    },
    "acpDrip": {
      "_doc": "createCliClient over the ACP transport against the port's fake ACP agent with fakeEnv set. On session/prompt the fake sends agent_thought_chunk thought, then each chunk of chunks as agent_message_chunk with gapMs between them (no permissions, no tool calls), then replies stopReason end_turn. The stream's text deltas must equal chunks exactly, one thought event must arrive, and the first text delta must arrive at least minLeadMs before done (two gaps = 400ms; a buffered stream has ~0ms lead). run() on the same client returns the concatenation.",
      "fakeEnv": {
        "TN_FAKE_DRIP": "1"
      },
      "thought": "pondering",
      "chunks": [
        "drip-1 ",
        "drip-2 ",
        "drip-3"
      ],
      "gapMs": 200,
      "minLeadMs": 300,
      "expectDoneText": "drip-1 drip-2 drip-3",
      "expectThought": {
        "type": "thought",
        "delta": "pondering",
        "via": "acp"
      }
    },
    "cliTransport": {
      "_doc": "The one-shot CLI transport does not stream incrementally for any style: the reply is the §8C JSON envelope, which is content OR tool_calls, and which one it is is known only once the whole reply has parsed. Streaming it would mean emitting text that may turn out to be a tool call. Stream still never errors: tool events as they happen, the whole answer as ONE text event, then done.",
      "incremental": {
        "claude": false,
        "codex": false,
        "copilot": false,
        "opencode": false,
        "devin": false,
        "gemini": false,
        "goose": false,
        "custom": false
      }
    }
  }
